        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports “sugars up & down” and “eyes a bit crusty.” For months, gritty/burning eyes bilaterally, worse in the morning, with crusting of the lids and mild redness. History of recurrent “styes.” Denies polyuria, polydipsia, weight loss, chest pain, shortness of breath, photophobia, decreased visual acuity, foreign-body sensation, purulent discharge, and severe pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
